Description: GtkGLArea: a plain area's deep picture on a surface of its own, the memory way, luminances and mastering data
 GTK 3 draws a window in 8 bit sRGB. A plain GtkGLArea (one that does not ask
 for stereo) whose format is deeper than 8 bits, whose colour state is not
 sRGB, or which carries luminances or mastering data now hands its picture to
 the compositor on the stereo area's own kind of surface, with nothing
 declared, so that its depth and its description reach the compositor; the
 window keeps its hole over it as for a stereo area. The new properties
 surface-shown and surface-error say whether it does and, where it cannot (an
 X window, a compositor without colour management), why: it is then drawn into
 its window as before.
 .
 On Wayland the picture goes to the compositor as a dma-buf where one carries
 it, and otherwise through memory: a wl_shm buffer of a format the compositor
 lists, as deep as the picture (XBGR16161616, XBGR2101010, XBGR16161616F,
 XBGR8888, or XRGB8888 with red and blue exchanged), read back every frame.
 That keeps every bit of a 16 bit picture on drivers that export no 16 bit
 dma-buf (NVIDIA's EGL, zink on NVIDIA's Vulkan driver) and gives a software
 renderer a way at all; a format no way carries fails as a format
 (GDK_GL_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED_FORMAT), so a program can take another.
 GDK_WAYLAND_GL_AREA_MEMORY=1 takes the memory way always, =0 never. The stereo
 protocol and libstereo-declare are needed for a stereo area only.
 .
 gtk_gl_area_set_luminances(), gtk_gl_area_set_mastering_display() and
 gtk_gl_area_set_content_light_levels() carry wp_color_management_v1's
 set_luminances, set_mastering_display_primaries, set_mastering_luminance,
 set_max_cll and set_max_fall (CTA-861-H, SMPTE ST 2086) into the surface's
 description, checked against the features the compositor lists and the
 protocol's own rules first (a maximum and a reference above the minimum).
 Without them a PQ picture is described with PQ's defaults (peak 10000 cd/m2)
 and a compositor that tone maps shows its reference white at about half.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: other, Sparky Stereo OS (queue row 137, GIMP milestone 3: the deep and HDR canvas)
Forwarded: no
