+ * ## Depth and colour ##
+ *
+ * GTK 3 draws a window in 8 bit sRGB. A plain area (one that does not ask
+ * for stereo) whose format is deeper, whose colour state is another, or
+ * which carries luminances or mastering data (gtk_gl_area_set_luminances(),
+ * gtk_gl_area_set_mastering_display(),
+ * gtk_gl_area_set_content_light_levels()) hands its picture to the
+ * compositor on the same kind of surface of its own, with nothing declared,
+ * so that its depth and its description reach the compositor
+ * (#GtkGLArea:surface-shown). Where that cannot be done (an X window, a
+ * compositor without colour management) it says why
+ * (#GtkGLArea:surface-error) and is drawn into its window.
+ *
+ * On Wayland the picture goes to the compositor as a dma-buf, or through
+ * memory (a wl_shm buffer of the picture's own depth) where no dma-buf
+ * carries it: a driver that exports none, or none of the picture's format.
+ *
  * In order to draw, you have to connect to the #GtkGLArea::render signal,
  * or subclass #GtkGLArea and override the @GtkGLAreaClass.render() virtual
  * function.
